BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: W.P.\(Civil\) No. 210 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: SCIN010090122026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Constitution Bench \(3 Judges\)

PARTIES:
Dr. Subhash Kashyap \(Constitutional Scholar\)
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
Union of India & Law Commission of India
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India, Special Marriage Act 1954

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
Article 14, Article 15, Article 21, Article 44

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Gender Justice, Matrimonial Equality, Article 44, Succession Rights, Law Commission

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Public interest litigation seeking uniform matrimonial property rights and maintenance standards for women regardless of religious denomination.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Does disparity in maintenance and succession laws across personal codes violate equality under Articles 14 and 15?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Gender justice and equal matrimonial protections are fundamental constitutional imperatives that transcend statutory distinctions.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Writ Petition Disposed; Law Commission requested to submit final report on inter-faith matrimonial equality within 6 months.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Constitution Bench \(3 Judges\)
Supreme Court of India
